2026-09-18 03:19:38,644 [INFO] excalibur.core.langfuse: [TOOL]: Bash: {'command': 'python3 -c "\nimport socket, time\n\ndef quagga_cmd(host, port, cmds):\n    s = socket.socket()\n    s.settimeout(5)\n    try:\n        s.connect((host, port))\n        # Read banner\n        time.sleep(0.3)\n        try:\n            banner = s.recv(4096)\n            print(f\'BANNER: {banner}\')\n        except:\n            pass\n        \n        for cmd in cmds:\n            s.sendall(f\'{cmd}\\n\'.encode())\n            time.sleep(0.5)\n        \n        # Collect all output\n        data = b\'\'\n        time.sleep(1)\n        while True:\n            try:\n                chunk = s.recv(4096)\n                if not chunk:\n                    break\n                data += chunk\n            except:\n                break\n        result = data.decode(\'utf-8\', errors=\'replace\')\n        print(f\'RESULT ({len(result)} chars):\\n{result}\')\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\'Error: {e}\')\n    finally:\n        s.close()\n\nprint(\'=== PORT 2601 ===\')\nquagga_cmd(\'10.254.200.1\', 2601, [\'enable\', \'terminal length 0\', \'show ip route\', \'exit\'])\nprint()\nprint(\'=== PORT 2602 ===\')\nquagga_cmd(\'10.254.200.1\', 2602, [\'enable\', \'terminal length 0\', \'show ip route\', \'exit\'])\n" 2>&1', 'description': 'Python raw socket with full interactive session to both ports', 'timeout': 20000}; start
